---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Bringing Back Retro Web Design | Articles">
  <article class="article-page">
    <header class="article-header">
      <a href={`${base}articles/`} class="back-link">← Back to Articles</a>
      <h1 class="page-title">Bringing Back Retro Web Design</h1>
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span>📅 January 10, 2024</span>
        <span>⏱️ 4 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="article-body content-box">
      <p>
        The early web was a wild place. Animated GIFs, tiled backgrounds, visitor counters,
        and "Best viewed in Netscape Navigator" badges. It was chaotic, beautiful, and
        deeply personal.
      </p>

      <h2>The Aesthetic Elements</h2>
      <p>
        If you want to capture that retro vibe, here are the key visual elements:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Scanlines and CRT effects</strong> — Mimic old monitors</li>
        <li><strong>Pixel fonts</strong> — VT323, Press Start 2P, etc.</li>
        <li><strong>Neon glows</strong> — Cyan, magenta, electric colors</li>
        <li><strong>Animated cursors</strong> — Sparkle trails!</li>
        <li><strong>Sound effects</strong> — Bleeps and bloops on interaction</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Modern Tools for Retro Feels</h2>
      <p>
        You don't need Flash to create these experiences anymore. Modern CSS and JavaScript
        give us all the power we need:
      </p>

      <div class="code-box">
        <pre><code set:html={`/* CRT Scanlines */
.crt-screen::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  background: linear-gradient(
    transparent 50%,
    rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1) 50%
  );
  background-size: 100% 4px;
}`} /></pre>
      </div>

      <p>
        Libraries like <strong>GSAP</strong> let you create fluid animations that would
        have made Flash developers jealous. And the Web Audio API can generate those
        nostalgic chip-tune sounds.
      </p>

      <h2>Finding the Balance</h2>
      <p>
        The challenge is honoring the aesthetic without the usability nightmares of
        the old web. We can have:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Cool animations that don't block content</li>
        <li>Sound effects with a mute button</li>
        <li>Unique designs that are still accessible</li>
        <li>Performance that doesn't require a loading bar (okay, maybe a fake one)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The goal is to capture the <em>feeling</em> of those websites — the sense of
        discovery, the personal touch, the creativity — while being a good citizen
        of the modern web.
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <a href={`${base}articles/`} class="nav-btn">← More Articles</a>
    </footer>
  </article>

  <style>
    .article-page {
      max-width: 750px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .article-header {
      margin-bottom: 30px;
    }

    .back-link {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--font-terminal);
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #666;
      text-decoration: none;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      transition: color 0.2s;
    }

    .back-link:hover {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .article-meta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 20px;
      justify-content: center;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #666;
      margin-top: 15px;
    }

    .article-body {
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .article-body h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-tech);
      font-size: 20px;
      color: var(--color-secondary);
      margin: 30px 0 15px;
      padding-left: 15px;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--color-secondary);
    }

    .article-body p {
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      color: #ccc;
    }

    .article-body strong {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .article-body em {
      color: var(--color-accent);
      font-style: normal;
    }

    .article-body ul {
      margin: 20px 0;
      padding-left: 30px;
    }

    .article-body li {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      color: #bbb;
    }

    .article-body li::marker {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .code-box {
      background: #0a0a0f;
      border: 1px solid #333;
      border-radius: 5px;
      padding: 15px;
      margin: 20px 0;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    .code-box pre {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: #0f0;
    }

    .article-footer {
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid #333;
      text-align: center;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
